{"id":"resp_a119779e36e877c8","created_at":1795550868,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9c517a826e8df925","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to repair the previous SHACL candidate. The issue: ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR - target classes select beyond declared population. The declared owner_class is https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship. So shapes should target only ship class, not other classes like QuantityValue, upperIceWaterlineCase etc? The admission scope error says \"Other target classes select beyond declared population\". Means that the shapes' sh:targetClass must be limited to the owner_class. The contract E134 indicates representation-only modelPaths: fromOwner ship to upperIceWaterlineCase via hasUpperIceWaterlineCase. Also owners mapping. target_owner is null currently. We need to constrain activation to the supplied population boundary: use sh:targetClass only ship, and for other shapes use sh:targetClass may be fine? The admission scope expects shapes only target ship? Probably only ship shape should be targetClass; other shapes are supportive and can be referenced via sh:node but not targeted globally. So we should remove sh:targetClass from QuantityValueShape and UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape, making them not have targetClass (or use sh:targetNode? but easier: remove targetClass declarations). However the instruction: \"Never remove constraints merely to silence a canonical-identifier error. Unit renaming is not numeric conversion. An old constraint may be excessive: supported removal is allowed but will require source-grounded change/removal assessment\". Here removing targetClass is acceptable because those shapes are auxiliary and not needed to be globally applied; they can be used via node constraints.\n\nAlso the second finding: UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT \"Target cannot be bound to an explicit model owner\" at sh:targetClass line 14 column 20 referencing QuantityValue. So we should remove that targetClass.\n\nThus modify the previous SHACL: For nltl:QuantityValueShape and nltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape, remove sh:targetClass statements. Keep properties.\n\nAlso ensure ship shape uses sh:targetClass ship (already). Ensure property path sh:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase uses sh:class and sh:node referencing UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape (still okay). Might need to ensure that the shape's target_class is ship and activation restricted accordingly.\n\nAlso need to possibly add sh:targetClass for upperIceWaterlineDisplacement? Already property path expects node.\n\nNo other errors.\n\nThus produce revised SHACL block.\n\nWe must keep other constraints unchanged. Provide entire revision.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_91c0b81921ba5008","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for QuantityValue (the representation of a numeric quantity)\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nnltl:QuantityValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    # NOTE: No global targetClass – activation is limited to contexts where the shape is referenced via sh:node.\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"A QuantityValue must have exactly one numericValue (decimal).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:class unit:KiloTON_Metric ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"A QuantityValue must specify the unit KiloTON_Metric (kt).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:message \"A QuantityValue representing displacement must have a decimal numericValue and unit kt.\" .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for upperIceWaterlineCase (design condition)\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nnltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    # NOTE: No global targetClass – the shape is applied via sh:node from the Ship shape.\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:waterlineCaseDisplacement ;\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"Each UpperIceWaterlineCase must have a waterlineCaseDisplacement expressed as a QuantityValue.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:message \"UpperIceWaterlineCase must provide displacement for the associated waterline case.\" .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for Ship (the primary focus class)\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nnltl:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    # Requirement: ship must be linked to at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ;\n        sh:class nltl:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node nltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape ;\n        sh:message \"A ship must have at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase (hasUpperIceWaterlineCase).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    # Requirement: ship displacement (DUI) expressed as upperIceWaterlineDisplacement\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:upperIceWaterlineDisplacement ;\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"A ship must have an upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (DUI) expressed as a QuantityValue.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    # NOTE: The UR I2.1.2.2 specifies that when multiple waterlines exist,\n    # the displacement used must be the greatest among them.  SHACL does\n    # not provide a native mechanism to compute a maximum across a set of\n    # values; therefore this aspect of the requirement is recorded as\n    # ambiguous and is not enforced by the shape.  Implementations may\n    # apply additional SPARQL-based SHACL constraints if required.\n    sh:message \"Ship must be linked to an UpperIceWaterlineCase and provide its displacement (DUI) in kt.\" .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Documentation of ambiguity\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ambiguityNote\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    rdfs:comment \"Ambiguity: The requirement 'where multiple waterlines are used, the displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest displacement' cannot be fully expressed in pure SHACL.  The shape therefore enforces the existence of the relevant properties but does not enforce the 'greatest displacement' selection rule.\" .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":23855,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":336,"cache_write_tokens":23504,"input_tokens_per_turn":[23855],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[336]},"output_tokens":1457,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":503,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1457],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":25312},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}